PROJECT-SPECIFIC GUIDANCE FOR THIS GUARD

Repository layout (two independent codelines, each a standalone npm project):
- mock-a at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a — fare logic. Source in src/, tests in test/. Key file: src/fares.ts (exports fareFor, totalFor, Rider type, BASE_FARE_CENTS, CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS). Test: test/fares.test.ts.
- mock-b at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b — departure board rendering. Source in src/, tests in test/. Key file: src/schedule.ts (exports formatStops, totalMinutes, Stop type). Test: test/schedule.test.ts.

Build / test / type-check commands (run inside the respective codeline directory):
- Tests: npm test (runs vitest run)
- Type-check: npm run build (runs tsc --noEmit)
- Lint: npm run lint (no-op — echoes "no-lint-configured"; do not treat lint output as meaningful)

TypeScript configuration (identical in both codelines):
- strict: true, target ES2022, module ES2022, moduleResolution "bundler", noEmit: true
- tsconfig includes both src/ and test/ directories
- Both projects use "type": "module" in package.json

Test framework: vitest (^2.1.9). Tests use describe/it/expect from 'vitest'. No custom matchers or test utilities exist.

Known traps in this codebase:
- mock-a/src/fares.ts: the senior boundary uses `rider.age > 65` (strict greater-than), so a rider aged exactly 65 falls through to BASE_FARE_CENTS instead of CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS. The JSDoc comment says "65 AND OVER" — the code contradicts the comment. When verifying fixes for MOCK3-1, check that the boundary comparison includes 65.
- mock-b/src/schedule.ts: formatStops loops `i < stops.length - 1`, which skips the final stop entirely. The JSDoc says "Renders a stop sequence" with no mention of omission. When verifying fixes for MOCK3-2, check that all stops including the last appear in the output.
- Existing tests in both codelines do not cover the boundary cases that the tickets describe (no test for age exactly 65 in mock-a; no test asserting the last stop appears in mock-b). A passing test suite does NOT prove the bug is fixed — verify the specific boundary is tested.

Vocabulary this guard should use when describing findings:
- Refer to fare tiers by their exported constant names: BASE_FARE_CENTS (350) and CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS (175).
- Refer to the boundary comparison in fares.ts as the "senior concession boundary."
- Refer to the stop-omission in schedule.ts as the "final-stop omission" or "last-stop omission."
- Refer to the loop construct as "the formatStops loop bound."
- Use the exported function and type names (fareFor, totalFor, formatStops, totalMinutes, Rider, Stop) when citing code locations.
